&lt;p&gt;Pianist and composer Amy Williams performs Morton Feldman&amp;rsquo;s&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Triadic Memories&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;(1981) is a 75-minute exploration of slowly evolving repetition, where exact repeats, minute variations, and subtle harmonic shifts invite deep, meditative listening. Williams first encountered Feldman&amp;rsquo;s music in childhood and has spent nearly three decades performing, studying, and recording his work. In honor of the 100th anniversary of his birth, Williams draws upon her extensive relationship with his music to bring rare depth and insight to this monumental solo composition.&lt;/p&gt;
